  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The big seaside meeting point for people from Toulon: four sandy coves (Lido, Mistral, de la Source, des Pins), a large tree-lined park, waterfront restaurants and over 1,300 free parking spaces. It's one of the busiest spots in the city, summer and winter alike.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>New update for 2026: the harmonised rules for the Mourillon beaches, set the previous year, were adjusted for summer 2026 — dogs on leash are now allowed year-round with no time restriction on the Promenade Henri-Fabre. Before this change, a stricter tolerance applied in summer (only 6am-8.30am in the morning, from 1 June to 31 August); that time window no longer applies since the 2026 update. In all cases, dogs remain banned on the sand, the lawns and the Plaine des Sports. Category 1 and 2 dogs must additionally be muzzled. Non-compliance with these rules is punishable by a €135 fine.</p>
      <p>Two dedicated dog areas round out the offering in the same area: a dog park with two off-leash enclosures (small dogs / medium-large dogs), and a swimming area reserved for dogs on the Anse Tabarly peninsula.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: these rules have already changed several times in recent years (last recorded update: the 2026 adjustment lifting the summer time restriction) — a look at the signs posted at the beach entrance remains the best guarantee, as the rules may still change from one season to the next.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Fort Saint-Louis and the Mourillon acclimatisation garden are just steps away, as are the Mourillon dog park and Anse Tabarly, to extend the outing after a walk by the sea.</p>
    </div>

